  "description": "Rear guard torus chess with crazyhouse's hand: a captured piece changes sides and may later be put back on the board as a move. A pawn comes back as a pawn facing forward, whichever way it faced when it was taken, onto the ranks in front of its army, so a rear guard that falls is not rebuilt. On chess the hand makes a sharp game sharper (crazyhouse); on a board with no corner to trap a king in it goes too far: every capture comes back, there are more than twice as many moves to choose from, and the lead changes hands more often than in any other wrapped game, which makes a sharp game but a hard one to read.",
